"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[868],{8822(n,o,t){t.r(o),t.d(o,{_pageData:()=>s,default:()=>r});var e=t(641);const s=JSON.parse('{"path":"/bagisto-connector/synchronization.html","title":"Synchronization","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"prev":"/bagisto-connector/general-settings.md"},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"bagisto-connector/synchronization.md"}'),a={name:"synchronization.md"},r=(0,t(6262).A)(a,[["render",function(n,o,t,s,a,r){return(0,e.uX)(),(0,e.CE)("div",null,[...o[0]||(o[0]=[(0,e.Fv)('<h1 id="synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#synchronization"><span>Synchronization</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Bulk Sync</strong> feature allows you to push existing WooCommerce data to Bagisto in batches. This is especially useful during the initial setup or if automatic synchronization was temporarily disabled.</p><p>Navigate to <strong>WC to Bagisto</strong> &gt; <strong>Bulk Sync</strong> to access this functionality.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/bulk-sync.png" alt="Bulk Sync"></p><hr><h2 id="how-bulk-synchronization-works" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-bulk-synchronization-works"><span>How Bulk Synchronization Works</span></a></h2><p>The plugin uses a background processing queue to handle bulk synchronizations. This ensures that your server is not overwhelmed and the process completes successfully without timing out, even when syncing thousands of records.</p><h3 id="process-flow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#process-flow"><span>Process Flow</span></a></h3><ol><li><strong>Select Entity:</strong> Choose what you want to sync (Categories, Products, Customers, Users, Orders, or Taxes).</li><li><strong>Filter/Exclude:</strong> (Optional) Provide specific IDs that you want to exclude from the sync process.</li><li><strong>Start Sync:</strong> Click the sync button. The plugin will fetch the relevant records and add them to the background queue.</li><li><strong>Background Processing:</strong> A cron job runs every 5 minutes to process the queued items in batches. You can monitor the progress through a live syncing bar in your dashboard.</li></ol><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/customer-syncing-bar.png" alt="Syncing Progress Bar"></p><hr><h2 id="available-synchronization-options" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#available-synchronization-options"><span>Available Synchronization Options</span></a></h2><h3 id="customer-user-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#customer-user-synchronization"><span>Customer &amp; User Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/customer-sync.png" alt="Customer Sync"></p><p>Sync your user base and customers.</p><ul><li><strong>Role Filtering:</strong> For users, you can include or exclude specific WordPress roles (e.g., exclude &#39;subscriber&#39; if you only want to sync admins).</li><li><strong>Default Values:</strong> Customers and users will inherit the default groups, roles, and statuses defined in the <strong>General Settings</strong>.</li></ul><h3 id="category-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#category-synchronization"><span>Category Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/category-sync.png" alt="Category Sync"></p><p>Synchronize your WooCommerce product categories to Bagisto.</p><ul><li><strong>Update Existing:</strong> You can choose whether to update categories that already exist in Bagisto or only create new ones.</li><li><strong>Hierarchy:</strong> The plugin attempts to maintain the parent-child relationship of categories during synchronization.</li></ul><h3 id="attribute-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#attribute-synchronization"><span>Attribute Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/attribute-sync.png" alt="Attribute Sync"></p><p>Synchronize your WooCommerce global attributes to Bagisto.</p><ul><li><strong>Terms &amp; Values:</strong> Ensures that all associated attribute terms are mapped properly.</li><li><strong>Consistency:</strong> Maintains data parity for variable product generation between the stores.</li></ul><h3 id="product-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#product-synchronization"><span>Product Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/product-sync.png" alt="Product Sync"></p><p>Push your WooCommerce products to Bagisto catalog.</p><ul><li><strong>Supported Types:</strong> Simple and Variable products are supported.</li><li><strong>Attributes:</strong> Product attributes, variations, and stock levels are included in the sync.</li><li><strong>Exclusions:</strong> Enter specific Product IDs separated by commas to skip them during the sync.</li></ul><h3 id="tax-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#tax-synchronization"><span>Tax Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/tax-sync.png" alt="Tax Sync"></p><p>Push your WooCommerce tax classes and rates to Bagisto.</p><ul><li><strong>Tax Mapping:</strong> Uses the defaults defined in settings to correctly categorize the synchronized tax rates.</li><li><strong>Automatic Rates:</strong> Syncs standard, reduced rate, and zero rate tax classes.</li></ul><h3 id="order-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#order-synchronization"><span>Order Synchronization</span></a></h3><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/order-sync.png" alt="Order Sync"></p><p>Push historical WooCommerce orders to Bagisto.</p><ul><li>Orders are synced with their line items, totals, and customer references.</li><li><strong>Prerequisite:</strong> Ensure that products and customers are synced <strong>before</strong> syncing orders to prevent missing references in Bagisto.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="selective-synchronization-via-bulk-actions" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#selective-synchronization-via-bulk-actions"><span>Selective Synchronization via Bulk Actions</span></a></h2><p>If you don&#39;t want to sync all records at once or wait for automatic synchronization, you can selectively sync specific items using native WooCommerce bulk actions.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/selective-sync.png" alt="Selective Sync"></p><ol><li>Navigate to the respective WooCommerce listing page (e.g., <strong>Products</strong>, <strong>Users</strong>, or <strong>Orders</strong>).</li><li>Use the checkboxes on the left to select the specific records you want to sync.</li><li>Click the <strong>Bulk actions</strong> dropdown at the top of the table.</li><li>Select <strong>Sync to Bagisto</strong> and click <strong>Apply</strong>.</li><li>The selected records will be instantly synchronized, and their respective <strong>Bagisto ID</strong> will be updated and displayed in the table column.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="automatic-synchronization" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#automatic-synchronization"><span>Automatic Synchronization</span></a></h2><p>In addition to bulk syncing, the plugin supports real-time automatic synchronization. If enabled in the <strong>Settings</strong>, any new entity created or updated in WooCommerce will instantly be pushed to Bagisto.</p><blockquote><p>[!IMPORTANT] Automatic synchronization relies on WooCommerce hooks. Ensure that your server can make fast external cURL requests, as this happens during the saving process.</p></blockquote><hr><h2 id="sync-completion-notifications" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#sync-completion-notifications"><span>Sync Completion &amp; Notifications</span></a></h2><p>Once a background bulk sync completes, you will see a success message in the admin interface. You can verify the detailed results of each batch by checking the <strong>Logs</strong>.</p>',48)])])}]])}}]);